# What travels and what does not.
#
# Travels: the manuscript sources, the workstream records, the reproducibility
# scripts, and the small JSON each run writes. Those are the evidence and the
# means to regenerate it, and they are worth reading in a diff.
#
# Also travels: one complete run of RQ2/run.sh, under RQ2/runs/.
# That directory is the evidence -- the environment, every command with its exit
# code and duration, the converted graphs, the result JSON and a summary. It
# weighs 840 KB, so there is no size reason to keep any of it off GitHub. Both
# converter versions are kept, because the paper reports a difference between
# them. The scratch checkouts under RQ2/work/ do not travel.
#
# Stays on the VM: run metrics, working conversion trees and LaTeX
# intermediates. The metrics are timing logs rather than evidence, the working
# trees are regenerable, and a git history of either is noise.

# --- converted RDF and conversion working state -------------------------------
**/run_metrics/
**/.intermediate/
*.nt
*.nt.gz
*.nt.br
*.hdt
*.hdt.index*
*.cottas
*.cottas.gz
*.ttl.gz
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
vcf_core_reviewed/

# --- LaTeX build products -----------------------------------------------------
.build/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
pdfa.xmpi

# --- macOS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# --- packaging ----------------------------------------------------------------
VCF-Core-SWAT4HCLS-2027*.zip

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- deliberately kept, despite the rules above -------------------------------
# The exported PDFs are the submission artifacts, so they stay tracked.
!main_long.pdf
!main_short.pdf
# One complete run is the evidence; the scratch it was built from is not.
RQ2/work/
# Pinned checkouts shared by every RQ script; fetched, never stored.
.artifacts/
# RQ1, RQ3 and RQ4 fetch what they evaluate here; the copies are not stored.
RQ1/work/
RQ3/work/
RQ4/work/
!RQ4/artifacts/
!RQ4/artifacts/**
!RQ1/results/
!RQ1/results/**
!RQ3/results/
!RQ3/results/**
!RQ2/runs/
!RQ2/runs/**
# The archived earlier runs, kept only so old commits stay interpretable.
!archive/
!archive/**
